WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.522
The original OpenHW naming deck used five fields: family, word length, class, identity, and an optional modifier.

2
00:00:06.522 --> 00:00:10.793
There the identity combined pipeline length with a product feature number.

3
00:00:10.793 --> 00:00:18.874
Current CVA6 documentation publishes a related but clearer pattern: C V, instruction length, class, pipeline stages, and product identifier.

4
00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:23.434
Both help parse names, but neither applies blindly to every current repository.

5
00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.800
The current manual remains authoritative.

